# `samples` is written as a union of nine classes of views. All have numbers for elements, so a holder of that type is a holder like that of one class:
# it is asked once whether it is as its class makes it (the class above them all: a bit of the cell), its length and its vector stand in front of the loop,
# and the element is a number, read inside the view. The operation names no kind: the code loads the type of the cell and goes by it. Nothing here hangs on who calls.
# f1 = total, f2 = fill
# -- source: a-view-written-as-a-union-of-kinds-is-read-and-stored-by-the-kind-of-its-cell.ts
